1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

﻿1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
- www.MY-SUBS.com -

2
00:00:07,541 --> 00:00:09,082
- Brace yourselves!
- Disa!

3
00:00:09,083 --> 00:00:11,499
[DWARVES EXCLAIMING]

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,749
[NARVI] <i>A fire-mountain awoke.</i>

5
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:14,332
<i>The ground-shakes... </i>

6
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:16,582
<i>it spread through the
bones of the Earth,</i>

7
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:18,582
<i>collapsing our sun-shafts,</i>

8
00:00:18,583 --> 00:00:20,082
<i>our ability to grow crops.</i>

9
00:00:20,083 --> 00:00:21,332
No, no, no.

10
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:24,249
These Rings will be beyond
any power yet devised

11
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:26,458
by Dwarf, or Man.

12
00:00:27,083 --> 00:00:29,040
They shall be Rings of Power.

13
00:00:29,041 --> 00:00:31,040
<i>Power to heal your mountain.</i>

14
00:00:31,041 --> 00:00:33,791
[ANNATAR] Bringing your father
a means of saving his kingdom

15
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:35,874
<i>might be just the way to
earn back his respect.</i>

16
00:00:35,875 --> 00:00:37,665
<i>Perhaps, even your inheritance.</i>

17
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:39,624
Did you just insult my father?

18
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:43,624
You speak ill of the Queen again,
it'll be you suffers an infirmity.

19
00:00:43,625 --> 00:00:45,375
Have I made myself plain?

20
00:00:46,291 --> 00:00:47,332
[MAN 1] <i>Queen of lies!</i>

21
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:48,540
[MAN 2] <i>She's unfit to rule!</i>

22
00:00:48,541 --> 00:00:50,624
[EÄRIEN] His dying words,
the King spoke to me,

23
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:53,790
and said it was from
this... she took counsel.

24
00:00:53,791 --> 00:00:55,915
This Elf-stone is your queen!

25
00:00:55,916 --> 00:00:58,207
- Silence!
- The <i>palantír</i> is mine. We need it.

26
00:00:58,208 --> 00:01:00,582
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]
- [ELENDIL GRUNTS]

27
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:02,124
[MAN] <i>Murderer!</i>

28
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:03,375
Dark magic!

29
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,332
[SHRIEKS]

30
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:09,875
Pharazôn! Pharazôn! Pharazôn!

31
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,332
[PEOPLE CHANTING] Pharazôn! Pharazôn!

32
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:15,540
Your High King believes
the Dwarves to be unworthy.

33
00:01:15,541 --> 00:01:18,540
In fact, he has forbidden the
forging of any more Rings at all.

34
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:20,750
We have not the time
to bandy words about,

35
00:01:20,751 --> 00:01:22,999
convincing him who is worthy of aid.

36
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,625
- [ANNATAR] What are you doing?
- I am telling him

37
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,374
that I am closing up the forge.

38
00:01:26,375 --> 00:01:28,415
You would lie to your High King?

39
00:01:28,416 --> 00:01:30,791
I would grant us the
space to complete our work.

40
00:01:31,625 --> 00:01:35,124
This power in Eregion, I don't trust it.

41
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:36,749
<i>You told me once,</i>

42
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:40,374
<i>the fate of Elves is decided
by wiser minds than our own.</i>

43
00:01:40,375 --> 00:01:43,124
<i>That to try and alter it,
to try and cheat death,</i>

44
00:01:43,125 --> 00:01:45,707
<i>might lead to an even
greater catastrophe.</i>

45
00:01:45,708 --> 00:01:47,707
<i>I keep wondering... </i>

46
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:49,665
<i>What if you were right?</i>

47
00:01:49,666 --> 00:01:52,249
[GALADRIEL] <i>A legion of Orcs
have marched into Elvish lands.</i>

48
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:53,457
That trail.

49
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:54,790
I gather it leads to...

50
00:01:54,791 --> 00:01:56,332
Eregion, my liege.

51
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:59,666
Word of this must reach the High
King before our host sails for Mordor.

52
00:02:00,791 --> 00:02:02,207
Over there.

53
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:04,958
[GALADRIEL] <i>Get to Lindon. I will
occupy them as long as I am able.</i>

54
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,083
<i>Take it.</i>

55
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:09,166
<i>Take it, Elrond.</i>

56
00:02:10,166 --> 00:02:12,041
[ORCS GRUNTING]

57
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:17,500
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

58
00:02:20,083 --> 00:02:22,750
[IN QUENYA] A star shines
on the hour of our meeting...

59
00:02:23,416 --> 00:02:25,125
Lady Galadriel.

60
00:02:29,291 --> 00:02:31,291
[OPENING THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:14,250
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:45,041
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

63
00:04:54,666 --> 00:04:55,666
[NARVI] This way, sire.

64
00:04:55,667 --> 00:04:59,624
As you can see, we're attempting
to dig a new access-shaft,

65
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:01,332
to try to reach the sunlight.

66
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:04,486
Uh, but thus far, our every effort

67
00:05:04,487 --> 00:05:06,957
has only made the
mountain more unstable.

68
00:05:06,958 --> 00:05:09,416
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

69
00:05:15,416 --> 00:05:16,416
[DWARVES GRUNT]

70
00:05:23,791 --> 00:05:24,916
Something the matter, sire?

71
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
No.

72
00:05:28,791 --> 00:05:31,833
No, all is shortly to be well.

73
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:33,875
[DWARF 2] Yep.

74
00:05:33,876 --> 00:05:35,250
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

75
00:06:01,166 --> 00:06:05,125
[KING DURIN BREATHING HEAVILY]

76
00:06:08,375 --> 00:06:10,957
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

77
00:06:10,958 --> 00:06:12,125
Dig here.

78
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:17,915
Sire. That's a foundation wall.

79
00:06:17,916 --> 00:06:21,166
- Take it down...
- Are you explaining Delve-craft to me?

80
00:06:25,416 --> 00:06:28,583
This is where we are meant
to dig. Now do as I say.

81
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:37,333
Give me your axe.

82
00:06:37,958 --> 00:06:39,583
- Father...
- Axe!

83
00:06:52,508 --> 00:06:53,541
[GRUNTS]

84
00:06:53,542 --> 00:06:56,708
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

85
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,666
[GRUNTS]

86
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:04,750
Narvi!

87
00:07:04,751 --> 00:07:07,000
Uh... Shift's over!

88
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,040
Go. Go!

89
00:07:10,041 --> 00:07:11,582
- [DWARF 1] That's good.
- [DWARF 2] Tell me twice.

90
00:07:11,583 --> 00:07:12,916
[KING DURIN GRUNTING]

91
00:07:29,125 --> 00:07:33,165
Sire. Don't you think you'd
better stop for some air?

92
00:07:33,166 --> 00:07:34,332
[GRUNTS]

93
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:36,958
It's not air we need, it's light.

94
00:07:39,666 --> 00:07:41,083
[RUMBLING]

95
00:07:44,291 --> 00:07:45,291
[NARVI] Sire! Don't!

96
00:07:45,291 --> 00:07:46,291
[PRINCE DURIN IV] Father, no!

97
00:07:46,958 --> 00:07:47,958
[GRUNTS]

98
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
[GASPS]

99
00:07:52,833 --> 00:07:53,875
[KING DURIN PANTING]

100
00:07:55,583 --> 00:07:56,791
[KING DURIN CHUCKLES]

101
00:07:58,708 --> 00:08:00,375
[EXHILARATING MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:08:05,625 --> 00:08:08,125
[KING DURIN] Next time
I order you to dig,

103
00:08:10,125 --> 00:08:11,208
you do so.

104
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,333
[SCOFFS]

105
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,625
[BOTH LAUGHING]

106
00:08:21,791 --> 00:08:23,499
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

107
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,541
Here. Here.

108
00:08:26,083 --> 00:08:27,665
[PRINCE DURIN IV] Right.
One, two, three, four.

109
00:08:27,666 --> 00:08:29,499
[KING DURIN] <i>Pity those who dwell above.</i>

110
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:30,958
<i>Slaves to the sun.</i>

111
00:08:32,916 --> 00:08:33,916
[DWARVES GRUNTING]

112
00:08:35,166 --> 00:08:38,208
<i>Chained to its ceaseless
rhythm of waking and sleep.</i>

113
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:40,458
[ALL GRUNTING]

114
00:08:51,458 --> 00:08:55,250
<i>In Khazad-dûm, we are
free of its tyranny.</i>

115
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:05,875
Here, we bring the sun to us.

116
00:09:07,958 --> 00:09:12,915
At last, it is daybreak once more

117
00:09:12,916 --> 00:09:14,249
in our mountain!

118
00:09:14,250 --> 00:09:16,416
[ALL CHEERING]

119
00:09:19,291 --> 00:09:21,040
Khazad...

120
00:09:21,041 --> 00:09:22,750
[DWARVES] Dûm!

121
00:09:26,458 --> 00:09:28,874
[CELEBRIMBOR] Dwarves and
Elves working together.

122
00:09:28,875 --> 00:09:31,207
It was said to be impossible.

123
00:09:31,208 --> 00:09:34,665
But our cooperation has
achieved this wonder.

124
00:09:34,666 --> 00:09:39,166
And today, we embark upon a new dream,

125
00:09:39,916 --> 00:09:42,790
to enshrine our friendship in stone.

126
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,375
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

127
00:09:45,625 --> 00:09:46,750
[CELEBRIMBOR] Narvi?

128
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:49,250
[CLEARS THROAT]

129
00:09:51,958 --> 00:09:53,583
Narvi's big moment.

130
00:09:55,875 --> 00:09:56,958
[NARVI] Behold...

131
00:10:02,208 --> 00:10:03,832
the Doors of Durin.

132
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:05,790
[ALL LAUGHING]

133
00:10:05,791 --> 00:10:08,625
The new West-gate of our mountain.

134
00:10:09,708 --> 00:10:12,833
Unbreachable. Visible only by moonlight.

135
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:18,875
And guarded by a password,
known only to friends.

136
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,125
Now, take note, smiths,

137
00:10:22,958 --> 00:10:25,749
watch Narvi very
closely while he's here.

138
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,082
Not only because he
is a masterful artist.

139
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:29,249
- [DWARF] Mm...
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

140
00:10:29,250 --> 00:10:32,832
He's also a notorious thief. Do
not let any jewels go missing.

141
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:34,332
[DWARVES AND ELVES LAUGHING]

142
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:37,165
[NARVI] Yeah, well, try
checking his pockets.

143
00:10:37,166 --> 00:10:39,207
- [ALL LAUGHING]
- [DWARF] Oh, no...

144
00:10:39,208 --> 00:10:41,000
To a lasting friendship...

145
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:44,915
between Elves and Dwarves.

146
00:10:44,916 --> 00:10:46,208
[ALL CHEERING]

147
00:10:46,875 --> 00:10:49,416
[NARVI] Hospitality's much appreciated.

148
00:10:57,041 --> 00:11:00,083
Too much? My remarks. [CHUCKLES]

149
00:11:00,708 --> 00:11:02,708
I encouraged you to keep it short.

150
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:05,874
Oh...

151
00:11:05,875 --> 00:11:07,458
Do not recall you saying that.

152
00:11:09,208 --> 00:11:12,000
Well, you do not always listen.

153
00:11:13,541 --> 00:11:15,541
Once you have an idea set in your head.

154
00:11:19,916 --> 00:11:21,625
Truth is, I should've spoken longer.

155
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:24,916
To credit your contributions.

156
00:11:26,458 --> 00:11:27,458
[SIGHS]

157
00:11:28,458 --> 00:11:29,625
Forgive me.

158
00:11:31,875 --> 00:11:33,916
I find it difficult to stay festive,

159
00:11:35,041 --> 00:11:38,125
when those most affected by
Mordor's rise are still suffering.

160
00:11:41,375 --> 00:11:42,750
Rings for Men?

161
00:11:49,541 --> 00:11:51,500
- I did not say anything about Rings.
- [SCOFFS]

162
00:11:52,291 --> 00:11:55,540
It is a game you play, is it not?

163
00:11:55,541 --> 00:11:59,124
Sowing seeds in others'
minds and then convincing them

164
00:11:59,125 --> 00:12:01,207
that the fruit is of their own thought.

165
00:12:01,208 --> 00:12:04,500
I thought our minds were as one in this.

166
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:09,374
Have you had a change of heart?

167
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:13,791
This is a night for Dwarves. Come.
We shall speak of Men tomorrow.

168
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:17,833
I would prefer to speak of them now.

169
00:12:22,125 --> 00:12:24,541
Much of the misery of Men
is of their own making.

170
00:12:26,916 --> 00:12:29,499
And I have been informed that
it was the Men of the Southlands

171
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:31,749
who aided Adar in his
conquest in the first place.

172
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:32,832
Only some of them.

173
00:12:32,833 --> 00:12:35,291
Many of the rest have
already been given new homes,

174
00:12:36,416 --> 00:12:39,541
by their own kind, from Númenor.

175
00:12:40,375 --> 00:12:42,249
Have you ever been to Númenor?

176
00:12:42,250 --> 00:12:43,958
[SIGHS] No.

177
00:12:45,208 --> 00:12:46,666
It is remarkable.

178
00:12:47,666 --> 00:12:48,958
But fractured.

179
00:12:50,166 --> 00:12:53,500
Ever teetering between glory and ruin.

180
00:12:55,166 --> 00:12:57,208
I fear Númenor.

181
00:12:58,416 --> 00:13:00,000
More than any land in Middle-earth.

182
00:13:02,416 --> 00:13:05,916
I had hoped our Rings
might make her stable.

183
00:13:07,208 --> 00:13:09,583
We cannot give Rings to Men.

184
00:13:10,208 --> 00:13:12,499
The risk of corruption
is simply too great.

185
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,040
Whatever problems we
might solve will be nothing

186
00:13:15,041 --> 00:13:16,749
against those we could create.

187
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:17,833
Yes.

188
00:13:18,708 --> 00:13:19,875
You are right.

189
00:13:20,958 --> 00:13:23,958
Of course. Men are
capable of great frailty.

190
00:13:26,875 --> 00:13:28,583
But when the darkness falls,

191
00:13:29,666 --> 00:13:34,666
there are always some
who rise forth and shine.

192
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:40,208
Eärendil, Tuor,

193
00:13:41,333 --> 00:13:43,833
Beren, son of Barahir.

194
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:48,916
Exactly what are you proposing?

195
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:53,125
We find Men we can trust.

196
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:58,290
The wisest, the most
noble, the purest of heart.

197
00:13:58,291 --> 00:14:02,749
From Númenor to Rhûn, we
identify nine Ring-bearers

198
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,582
of the nine greatest mortal kingdoms.

199
00:14:04,583 --> 00:14:05,666
Nine?

200
00:14:08,125 --> 00:14:09,791
The perfection of the Three.

201
00:14:12,083 --> 00:14:13,541
Thrice perfected.

202
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:20,333
For our third forging,
we will make nine.

203
00:14:23,375 --> 00:14:28,416
We have accomplished
great things, my friend.

204
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:33,833
Let us not tempt failure...

205
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:39,541
by allowing our reach
to exceed our grasp.

206
00:14:44,041 --> 00:14:47,041
I am sorry. My answer is no.

207
00:14:48,416 --> 00:14:50,916
The Rings of Power are complete.

208
00:14:52,125 --> 00:14:53,208
Of course.

209
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:59,541
You need not apologize. Very well.

210
00:15:09,291 --> 00:15:11,500
I shall make the Nine myself.

211
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:24,875
[AR-PHARAZÔN] Have you ever
seen it? Across our western seas.

212
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:27,790
The white tower of Eressëa...

213
00:15:27,791 --> 00:15:31,041
the very gateway to the Undying Lands.

214
00:15:31,875 --> 00:15:33,375
I have not.

215
00:15:34,083 --> 00:15:35,708
[AR-PHARAZÔN] Only the keenest eye can.

216
00:15:37,458 --> 00:15:40,041
And only from the
peak of the Meneltarma.

217
00:15:40,666 --> 00:15:42,958
I reckon the Elves placed
it there on purpose.

218
00:15:43,458 --> 00:15:48,083
So that every sunset serves as
a reminder that our days must end

219
00:15:49,083 --> 00:15:50,625
and theirs will not.

220
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:54,499
That no matter how high we climb,

221
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:58,083
some things will be forever
withheld from our grasp.

222
00:16:02,625 --> 00:16:05,375
The Scepter is now in yours, Father.

223
00:16:07,291 --> 00:16:08,832
Is that not high enough?

224
00:16:08,833 --> 00:16:12,333
All my life, I believed it was.

225
00:16:20,333 --> 00:16:22,999
The Scepter is what you make it.

226
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,582
The Age of Men is upon
us, Father. Let us take it.

227
00:16:26,583 --> 00:16:30,291
Let us build the Númenor you have
always seen in your mind's eye.

228
00:16:40,250 --> 00:16:42,832
Once, when you were at her breast,

229
00:16:42,833 --> 00:16:47,875
your mother prophesied that
you would come to ill ends.

230
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,208
My mother?

231
00:16:57,166 --> 00:16:58,790
What did she say?

232
00:16:58,791 --> 00:17:03,165
Impress me in the task that
I am about to place upon you

233
00:17:03,166 --> 00:17:04,375
and I will tell you.

234
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,895
Fail to do so,

235
00:17:05,896 --> 00:17:09,875
and I shall have to find other
places to make use of you.

236
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:17,499
[NÚMENÓREANS CHANTING]
Pharazôn! Pharazôn! Pharazôn!

237
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,083
Pharazôn! Pharazôn! Pharazôn!

238
00:17:20,708 --> 00:17:21,708
[MÍRIEL] Listen to them.

239
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,540
[ELENDIL] There are
other voices out there.

240
00:17:24,541 --> 00:17:26,624
Valandil tells me that
in the Old Quarter,

241
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:28,875
prayers ascend night and day for you.

242
00:17:30,041 --> 00:17:31,333
For their Queen.

243
00:17:33,375 --> 00:17:35,082
Our Queen.

244
00:17:35,083 --> 00:17:37,624
Command us all and together
we can put this right.

245
00:17:37,625 --> 00:17:39,707
- The Sea-Guard is still loyal to you.
- Elendil...

246
00:17:39,708 --> 00:17:41,958
- Together we can fight.
- Elendil.

247
00:17:53,958 --> 00:17:58,250
It was you, who opened my heart
again to the way of The Faithful.

248
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:01,249
We swore to keep serving.

249
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:02,583
Now, you wish to be still...

250
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:05,416
while the wolves are licking the cradle?

251
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:10,000
What did you see? In the <i>palantír.</i>

252
00:18:17,416 --> 00:18:18,541
[ELENDIL] <i>I saw myself.</i>

253
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:22,291
<i>Lost.</i>

254
00:18:24,125 --> 00:18:25,541
<i>Riding from the city to... </i>

255
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:32,250
I know not where.

256
00:18:32,916 --> 00:18:35,125
Then you did not see it.

257
00:18:36,041 --> 00:18:38,166
- See what?
- Perhaps it's changed.

258
00:18:38,791 --> 00:18:40,000
What do you mean?

259
00:18:41,416 --> 00:18:43,790
Not every battle must
be fought to be won.

260
00:18:43,791 --> 00:18:45,815
Sometimes maintaining stillness of heart

261
00:18:45,816 --> 00:18:47,415
is the greatest victory of all,

262
00:18:47,416 --> 00:18:50,457
the greatest act of
faith one can perform.

263
00:18:50,458 --> 00:18:51,958
I don't understand.

264
00:18:54,375 --> 00:18:57,957
For years, that <i>palantír</i>

265
00:18:57,958 --> 00:19:00,540
has shown me only our island's downfall.

266
00:19:00,541 --> 00:19:03,540
But when you touched
it, that vision was gone.

267
00:19:03,541 --> 00:19:05,500
Changed to a new path.

268
00:19:06,166 --> 00:19:09,665
Pharazôn's kingship
is a part of that path.

269
00:19:09,666 --> 00:19:11,957
And so are you.

270
00:19:11,958 --> 00:19:14,458
You have asked for my command.

271
00:19:17,458 --> 00:19:18,708
Now it is given.

272
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:25,625
[BREATH TREMBLING]

273
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:30,999
No matter how hard they push you,
no matter what they try and take,

274
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,250
you must not jeopardize
Númenor's new destiny.

275
00:19:35,083 --> 00:19:38,500
You must remain the
calm at the storm's eye.

276
00:19:39,166 --> 00:19:41,416
Go back to your ship, Captain.

277
00:19:43,458 --> 00:19:44,708
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

278
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:51,291
- [NÚMENÓREAN GUARD 1] You render it willingly?
- [MAN] I do.

279
00:19:51,292 --> 00:19:53,458
[NÚMENÓREAN GUARD 1] You're
no longer a Sea-Guard. Next.

280
00:19:55,583 --> 00:19:56,583
[NÚMENÓREAN GUARD 2] Line up.

281
00:19:57,083 --> 00:19:58,249
[ELENDIL] Lieutenant.

282
00:19:58,250 --> 00:19:59,416
All right. This way.

283
00:20:04,416 --> 00:20:06,000
What's the meaning of all this?

284
00:20:06,791 --> 00:20:11,040
Anyone deemed loyal to the
Queen-regent has been stripped of rank.

285
00:20:11,041 --> 00:20:12,540
On whose authority?

286
00:20:12,541 --> 00:20:13,833
[EÄRIEN] On mine.

287
00:20:18,125 --> 00:20:19,915
I'm sorry. I'd hoped
to tell you earlier.

288
00:20:19,916 --> 00:20:23,250
Lord Belzagar wanted the lot
of you charged with treason.

289
00:20:24,208 --> 00:20:28,290
And yet, overthrowing a queen
has earned you a promotion.

290
00:20:28,291 --> 00:20:30,958
How dare you reduce my
grief to petty ambition?

291
00:20:31,708 --> 00:20:35,082
My brother is dead because
Míriel peeped into an Elf-stone.

292
00:20:35,083 --> 00:20:37,665
You mock that which is sacred.

293
00:20:37,666 --> 00:20:40,082
[EÄRIEN] I mock that which is absurd.

294
00:20:40,083 --> 00:20:41,541
Ar-Pharazôn is your king.

295
00:20:42,208 --> 00:20:43,833
Accept it, Father. I beg you.

296
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:47,583
You are walking a treacherous path.

297
00:20:48,916 --> 00:20:50,957
And yours is made of seawater.

298
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:54,666
Take care to keep your feet beneath
you, it's a long way to the bottom.

299
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:01,749
- [WOMAN] Are you ready?
- [NÚMENÓREAN GUARD] Is everything there?

300
00:21:01,750 --> 00:21:03,208
- [MAN] Yes.
- [NÚMENÓREAN GUARD] Next.

301
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:06,750
It's all there. This is all
from the same. Check him up, now.

302
00:21:14,375 --> 00:21:15,583
Captain leaving deck!

303
00:21:18,041 --> 00:21:19,625
He's nobody's captain now.

304
00:21:24,916 --> 00:21:26,082
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:21:26,083 --> 00:21:27,083
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

306
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:41,333
He's right.

307
00:21:48,375 --> 00:21:49,375
I'm not.

308
00:21:54,875 --> 00:21:55,875
Captain.

309
00:22:00,875 --> 00:22:02,582
- Thank you, Captain.
- The Valar protect you.

310
00:22:02,583 --> 00:22:03,583
[KEMEN] That's enough.

311
00:22:03,584 --> 00:22:05,540
- [MAN 1] Thank you, Captain.
- [MAN 2] Thank you, Captain.

312
00:22:05,541 --> 00:22:07,749
- [MAN 3] Valar bless you, Captain.
- [MAN 3] Captain, thank you, sir.

313
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:09,207
- [MAN 4] Valar bless you.
- [MAN 5] Thank you, sir.

314
00:22:09,208 --> 00:22:10,666
[MAN 6] Thank you, Captain.

315
00:22:11,750 --> 00:22:12,999
That's enough.

316
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,999
- [MAN 7] Thank you, Captain.
- [MAN 8] Thank you, Captain.

317
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,082
How do you think this ends? Silence!

318
00:22:17,083 --> 00:22:20,625
- [MAN 9] Thank you, Captain. Thank you.
- [MAN 10] Bless you, Captain. Bless you.

319
00:22:22,416 --> 00:22:25,000
- [MAN 11] Captain, Elendil.
- [MAN 12] Valar bless you.

320
00:22:26,416 --> 00:22:27,416
[EÄRIEN] Valandil.

321
00:22:28,125 --> 00:22:30,250
Perhaps I can have
you taken off the list.

322
00:22:31,250 --> 00:22:32,375
I'll speak to the king.

323
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,750
You would do that for me?

324
00:22:37,833 --> 00:22:39,583
You're one of my oldest friends.

325
00:22:40,458 --> 00:22:44,625
I think you've made it clear
enough who your friends are.

326
00:22:57,541 --> 00:23:00,083
[CAPTIVATING MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,124
[CELEBRIMBOR] <i>Most noble High King.</i>

328
00:23:35,125 --> 00:23:38,165
<i>I write this letter
to convey my deep joy</i>

329
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:41,833
<i>on hearing of the success of
the Three Rings in Lindon.</i>

330
00:23:42,791 --> 00:23:48,125
<i>As requested, the forge is
dark and the workshop is empty.</i>

331
00:23:48,791 --> 00:23:51,154
<i>A precious calm has
settled over the city,</i>

332
00:23:51,155 --> 00:23:54,041
<i>and I foresee brighter days ahead.</i>

333
00:23:54,583 --> 00:23:57,374
<i>I hope you are able
to make a visit soon.</i>

334
00:23:57,375 --> 00:24:00,915
<i>Until then, I remain as ever,</i>

335
00:24:00,916 --> 00:24:04,875
<i>your loyal servant, Lord Celebrimbor.</i>

336
00:24:09,916 --> 00:24:11,915
[COMMANDER OF THE SOUTH] Our
armada is ready to depart.

337
00:24:11,916 --> 00:24:13,040
What are we waiting for?

338
00:24:13,041 --> 00:24:15,207
All is well in Eregion.

339
00:24:15,208 --> 00:24:17,707
The letter proves Galadriel was wrong.

340
00:24:17,708 --> 00:24:22,083
And whilst we hesitate, Adar's
army grows stronger by the day.

341
00:24:22,625 --> 00:24:25,375
If we are to invade, we must leave now.

342
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:28,125
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:24:30,250 --> 00:24:32,250
[HIGH-PITCHED TRILLING]

344
00:24:37,375 --> 00:24:39,499
[TRILLING DIES DOWN]

345
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:41,416
Our enemy is in Mordor.

346
00:24:42,458 --> 00:24:45,290
Are you truly prepared to
wager the future of Middle-earth

347
00:24:45,291 --> 00:24:47,833
on the whispers of that Ring alone?

348
00:24:50,625 --> 00:24:52,625
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

349
00:24:57,333 --> 00:24:59,333
- You pushed for this.
- [DISA] I know.

350
00:25:00,250 --> 00:25:03,333
- From the beginning.
- I know. I did. I know.

351
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:09,165
But learning to hear the
mountain's a gift from Aulë,

352
00:25:09,166 --> 00:25:12,875
one that's honed and
refined over a lifetime.

353
00:25:13,958 --> 00:25:14,958
And this it...

354
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:19,000
It feels somehow like cheating.

355
00:25:19,708 --> 00:25:21,041
Yeah, he's Durin the Third.

356
00:25:21,958 --> 00:25:24,583
I think he knows a thing
or two about wielding power.

357
00:25:25,083 --> 00:25:29,207
That kind of power would test
even the most virtuous of Dwarves.

358
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:31,291
I pray your father keeps his path true.

359
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:45,707
Oh! It's perfect.

360
00:25:45,708 --> 00:25:46,708
[PRINCE DURIN IV] Mmm-hmm.

361
00:25:47,458 --> 00:25:49,124
Two hundred for that one.

362
00:25:49,125 --> 00:25:51,082
Two hundred? For a bloody rock?

363
00:25:51,083 --> 00:25:53,165
It's a tuning crystal.

364
00:25:53,166 --> 00:25:56,915
I don't care if it's a cart
and six horses. I won't pay it.

365
00:25:56,916 --> 00:25:58,749
Ah, blame the king's new law.

366
00:25:58,750 --> 00:26:01,874
For every coin spent,
another goes to the crown.

367
00:26:01,875 --> 00:26:03,708
Ring tribute, he calls it.

368
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,375
Ring tribute?

369
00:26:06,875 --> 00:26:10,165
Sir, this is for our wee
girl's birthday next week.

370
00:26:10,166 --> 00:26:13,040
Spare a bit for her
sake? We'll give you 100.

371
00:26:13,041 --> 00:26:15,291
- One hundred?
- One hundred.

372
00:26:16,375 --> 00:26:17,375
How's that sound?

373
00:26:17,376 --> 00:26:19,666
Like mine shaft robbery.

374
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:24,500
[PRINCE DURIN IV GROANS SOFTLY]

375
00:26:26,041 --> 00:26:27,249
[DISA] Mmm!

376
00:26:27,250 --> 00:26:28,291
Hundred and fifty?

377
00:26:33,583 --> 00:26:34,708
[CHUCKLES]

378
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:36,582
Oh!

379
00:26:36,583 --> 00:26:38,707
- [DWARF] Careful.
- Aulë's beard, excuse me.

380
00:26:38,708 --> 00:26:40,500
It's rollin'. It's rollin'.

381
00:26:42,625 --> 00:26:44,333
You seem to have kicked it.

382
00:26:45,208 --> 00:26:47,541
Madam, I'm so sorry to get in your way.

383
00:26:48,208 --> 00:26:51,833
I have it, I have it, I
have it. Oof! No, I don't.

384
00:26:55,708 --> 00:26:56,708
[SIGHS]

385
00:27:01,208 --> 00:27:02,208
[GRUNTS]

386
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:04,250
[GRUNTS]

387
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:07,458
[GRUNTING]

388
00:27:13,083 --> 00:27:14,083
Now then...

389
00:27:14,708 --> 00:27:16,291
Where are you, you little...

390
00:27:21,041 --> 00:27:22,041
Oh! [ECHOING]

391
00:27:24,083 --> 00:27:25,083
What?

392
00:27:26,250 --> 00:27:27,958
What is this? [ECHOING]

393
00:27:30,708 --> 00:27:31,750
[GASPS]

394
00:27:37,708 --> 00:27:39,499
[VOCALIZING]

395
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,250
[ECHOING]

396
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:49,665
[CHUCKLES]

397
00:27:49,666 --> 00:27:51,249
There you are.

398
00:27:51,250 --> 00:27:53,000
[GRUNTING]

399
00:27:57,416 --> 00:27:58,540
Hmm.

400
00:27:58,541 --> 00:28:02,375
[CREATURE BELLOWING]

401
00:28:06,125 --> 00:28:07,125
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

402
00:28:07,875 --> 00:28:10,125
[CREATURE BELLOWING]

403
00:28:16,416 --> 00:28:18,250
[CREATURE ROARS]

404
00:28:18,833 --> 00:28:20,708
[SCREAMS]

405
00:28:24,208 --> 00:28:27,500
[KING DURIN] Emissaries of
the seven Dwarven realms,

406
00:28:28,416 --> 00:28:32,750
I have gathered you all here today
because Middle-earth is changing.

407
00:28:34,666 --> 00:28:36,333
Its limbs are stretching.

408
00:28:37,125 --> 00:28:39,583
Its bones, creaking.

409
00:28:41,458 --> 00:28:45,500
Some dark will threatens
all our kingdoms.

410
00:28:48,291 --> 00:28:53,000
But by Aulë's favor, my
people have passed this test.

411
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,375
And soon, yours shall pass it too.

412
00:28:58,333 --> 00:29:01,333
And rise together into
a new age for our kind

413
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:07,665
with the help of a power
that will change everything.

414
00:29:07,666 --> 00:29:09,000
[MURMURING]

415
00:29:10,708 --> 00:29:12,166
Seven Rings.

416
00:29:14,083 --> 00:29:15,583
Seven lords.

417
00:29:17,333 --> 00:29:22,041
And bound within each... power.

418
00:29:24,166 --> 00:29:25,625
Power over earth.

419
00:29:27,083 --> 00:29:28,083
Power over rock.

420
00:29:29,166 --> 00:29:32,208
Power to shape the destinies
of all Dwarves forever.

421
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,165
[EMISSARY GRUNTS]

422
00:29:35,166 --> 00:29:38,582
The Rings are not for
you, but for your masters.

423
00:29:38,583 --> 00:29:41,109
Go back and tell them
that each of your realms

424
00:29:41,110 --> 00:29:43,208
may share in this bounty.

425
00:29:45,833 --> 00:29:47,416
But it comes with a price.

426
00:29:49,125 --> 00:29:51,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:29:58,875 --> 00:30:01,083
[KING DURIN] <i>Khazad-dûm
shall never want again.</i>

428
00:30:03,916 --> 00:30:06,333
<i>There is gold right beneath us.</i>

429
00:30:10,833 --> 00:30:13,499
We should be delving much deeper.

430
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:16,207
But who set these restrictions?

431
00:30:16,208 --> 00:30:19,500
Well, you did, sire. Decades ago.

432
00:30:20,958 --> 00:30:22,041
Then strike them.

433
00:30:22,750 --> 00:30:23,790
Strike... But, sire...

434
00:30:23,791 --> 00:30:27,500
Strike them, Delve-master,
or I'll find them...

435
00:30:30,916 --> 00:30:32,665
- Where is it?
- You took it off.

436
00:30:32,666 --> 00:30:34,457
Where is it? What have you done with it?

437
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:37,375
It's there, sire.
You... You took it off.

438
00:30:38,083 --> 00:30:41,915
You said your hand was feeling heavy.

439
00:30:41,916 --> 00:30:43,500
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

440
00:30:44,125 --> 00:30:45,125
Oh...

441
00:30:46,250 --> 00:30:47,250
Hmm.

442
00:30:47,875 --> 00:30:50,458
It was. It was.

443
00:31:02,125 --> 00:31:03,125
[SIGHS]

444
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:08,291
Start to dig, points where I've marked.

445
00:31:09,625 --> 00:31:10,625
[NARVI] Sire.

446
00:31:15,250 --> 00:31:16,250
Stop!

447
00:31:18,041 --> 00:31:19,541
[BREATH TREMBLING]

448
00:31:21,750 --> 00:31:23,207
There's something under the mines.

449
00:31:23,208 --> 00:31:25,374
Disa heard it herself.

450
00:31:25,375 --> 00:31:29,458
A nameless evil, ancient and powerful.

451
00:31:30,625 --> 00:31:32,500
You mustn't dig.

452
00:31:36,750 --> 00:31:38,916
You have your orders, Delve-master.

453
00:31:40,583 --> 00:31:42,000
Narvi, I beg you.

454
00:31:43,958 --> 00:31:46,958
Delve-master. You have your orders.

455
00:31:50,916 --> 00:31:52,041
[NARVI SIGHS WEARILY]

456
00:31:54,875 --> 00:31:56,166
[DOOR OPENS]

457
00:31:57,541 --> 00:31:58,582
[DOOR CLOSES]

458
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:02,333
[KING DURIN] Stone-singers
speak of hearing the mountain.

459
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:08,791
- What?
- With this Ring, I can see it.

460
00:32:11,041 --> 00:32:15,332
Every shaft, every ore, every jewel.

461
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:17,750
In thousands of years,

462
00:32:18,541 --> 00:32:23,541
we have barely taken a thimble
from the ocean of her riches.

463
00:32:24,416 --> 00:32:26,208
Disa is mistaken.

464
00:32:29,625 --> 00:32:31,041
There is no danger.

465
00:32:36,083 --> 00:32:38,041
[CELEBRIMBOR BREATHING HEAVILY]

466
00:32:42,458 --> 00:32:43,541
- [MIRDANIA] My lord.
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING]

467
00:32:44,875 --> 00:32:45,875
[FEMALE ELF] Are you hurt?

468
00:32:47,375 --> 00:32:49,375
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

469
00:32:50,666 --> 00:32:51,832
[MALE ELF] Are you all right?

470
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:53,541
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

471
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:10,458
[CLATTERING]

472
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:18,125
Do my eyes deceive me?

473
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:22,458
No.

474
00:33:23,333 --> 00:33:25,500
We were casting a new design for a Ring.

475
00:33:26,041 --> 00:33:28,832
Mirdania was attempting
to resize it when...

476
00:33:28,833 --> 00:33:30,458
- [CLANKING]
- [ALL GASP]

477
00:33:33,875 --> 00:33:35,083
Where is she?

478
00:33:35,833 --> 00:33:36,833
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

479
00:33:38,666 --> 00:33:40,458
- Look out!
- [FEMALE DWARF] Master!

480
00:33:44,500 --> 00:33:45,540
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

481
00:33:45,541 --> 00:33:46,541
Get back!

482
00:33:52,291 --> 00:33:54,291
[BREATH TREMBLING]

483
00:33:54,833 --> 00:33:57,415
[DISEMBODIED VOICES WHISPERING]

484
00:33:57,416 --> 00:33:58,665
[MIRDANIA GASPS]

485
00:33:58,666 --> 00:33:59,750
[CELEBRIMBOR] Stop.

486
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,166
Breathe.

487
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,249
What happened?

488
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:13,541
I was in a place like this,

489
00:34:13,666 --> 00:34:19,666
but shrouded in mist
and darkness, and...

490
00:34:20,208 --> 00:34:21,875
I saw... I...

491
00:34:24,041 --> 00:34:27,083
At first, I thought it
was the forge burning.

492
00:34:30,875 --> 00:34:32,125
But it wasn't.

493
00:34:32,708 --> 00:34:33,708
What was it?

494
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,833
It was tall...

495
00:34:38,458 --> 00:34:41,458
and its skin was made of flames.

496
00:34:44,333 --> 00:34:50,082
It came toward me,
breathing, reeking of death,

497
00:34:50,083 --> 00:34:52,083
and I saw... I...

498
00:34:53,125 --> 00:34:54,750
I saw its eyes.

499
00:34:56,333 --> 00:34:58,958
Pitiless and eternal.

500
00:34:59,666 --> 00:35:01,083
I think it's been here.

501
00:35:02,250 --> 00:35:04,665
I think it's been here
among us, all along!

502
00:35:04,666 --> 00:35:06,250
You are with us now.

503
00:35:07,666 --> 00:35:09,333
There is nothing to fear.

504
00:35:11,958 --> 00:35:13,458
Look around.

505
00:35:15,666 --> 00:35:16,916
All is well.

506
00:35:20,208 --> 00:35:24,208
What did you do differently this time?

507
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:32,375
The Lord of Gifts shared your
worry that Men are too corruptible.

508
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:36,332
So, we sought to fortify the alloy
by adding more <i>mithril.</i>

509
00:35:36,333 --> 00:35:37,665
No, no!

510
00:35:37,666 --> 00:35:39,916
If you'd wanted to do
that, you should've...

511
00:35:41,958 --> 00:35:43,208
You...

512
00:35:47,791 --> 00:35:50,249
It would save us
immeasurable hours of toil

513
00:35:50,250 --> 00:35:55,166
if you would offer this
one, single word of counsel.

514
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,416
- My lord, Celebrimbor.
- You should...

515
00:36:11,125 --> 00:36:14,790
Forgive me, my lord, but Durin the
Younger is arrived from Khazad-dûm.

516
00:36:14,791 --> 00:36:16,083
No, tell him to wait.

517
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:21,041
He says it is urgent.
Something about the Rings.

518
00:36:23,250 --> 00:36:24,665
I will see what he wants.

519
00:36:24,666 --> 00:36:25,833
No.

520
00:36:27,416 --> 00:36:29,750
No. I will go.

521
00:36:40,083 --> 00:36:41,207
How do you mean "changed"?

522
00:36:41,208 --> 00:36:45,082
It's like he's colder. Quicker to anger.

523
00:36:45,083 --> 00:36:48,040
Now they tell me, he refuses
to share the other Rings

524
00:36:48,041 --> 00:36:52,832
unless the Dwarf-lords promise
him half a share of their mines!

525
00:36:52,833 --> 00:36:55,833
Now, greed is not his
way. It never has been.

526
00:36:56,666 --> 00:36:57,708
I... [SIGHS]

527
00:37:02,083 --> 00:37:05,207
Is it possible the Ring he's wearing...

528
00:37:05,208 --> 00:37:06,583
No.

529
00:37:08,166 --> 00:37:10,624
We used the same process, Durin,

530
00:37:10,625 --> 00:37:13,625
the same materials, even the
same tools as for the Three.

531
00:37:14,875 --> 00:37:19,416
Now, there simply cannot
be a fault in your Rings.

532
00:37:22,416 --> 00:37:25,000
Then maybe, the fault's
in the Ring-maker.

533
00:37:26,416 --> 00:37:27,582
What do you mean?

534
00:37:27,583 --> 00:37:31,416
How much do you really
know about this Annatar?

535
00:37:37,708 --> 00:37:39,708
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

536
00:37:46,791 --> 00:37:48,208
[ANNATAR] You are very brave.

537
00:37:49,458 --> 00:37:51,305
Some who behold the Unseen world

538
00:37:51,306 --> 00:37:54,833
are never quite at
home in this one again.

539
00:37:57,041 --> 00:37:58,707
[IN SINDARIN] Have you seen it?

540
00:37:58,708 --> 00:38:00,250
[IN ENGLISH] Yes.

541
00:38:01,875 --> 00:38:05,958
In its light, things
appear as they truly are.

542
00:38:07,375 --> 00:38:11,000
Beings of differing shades of light...

543
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:15,291
And its darkness.

544
00:38:18,375 --> 00:38:20,083
It pains me to say,

545
00:38:21,208 --> 00:38:23,583
for what you saw, I did not
wish for any of you to see

546
00:38:25,041 --> 00:38:26,875
until I had helped him to heal.

547
00:38:29,291 --> 00:38:34,875
You... You speak of... Lord Celebrimbor?

548
00:38:35,750 --> 00:38:36,958
Yes.

549
00:38:39,250 --> 00:38:41,165
The toll that creation
has exacted from him

550
00:38:41,166 --> 00:38:45,833
in crafting the Three and the
Seven has left him diminished.

551
00:38:46,708 --> 00:38:48,291
Vulnerable to the shadow.

552
00:38:52,541 --> 00:38:54,125
[IN SINDARIN] Then, what I saw...

553
00:38:55,458 --> 00:38:57,583
[IN ENGLISH] Promise me you'll
speak to none other of it.

554
00:38:58,500 --> 00:38:59,874
Including him.

555
00:38:59,875 --> 00:39:01,125
I promise.

556
00:39:07,458 --> 00:39:08,791
How strange.

557
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:12,500
When the light caught your hair,

558
00:39:14,291 --> 00:39:16,291
for a moment, you seemed
her perfect likeness.

559
00:39:17,708 --> 00:39:19,041
Whose likeness?

560
00:39:20,500 --> 00:39:22,166
Why, Lady Galadriel's, of course.

561
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:45,582
[HIGH PRIEST] The souls of those
we have lost yearn for peace.

562
00:39:45,583 --> 00:39:49,083
Tonight, we will help them to find it.

563
00:39:49,958 --> 00:39:54,165
Until we meet again in
the far green country

564
00:39:54,166 --> 00:39:56,583
under a swift sunrise.

565
00:39:58,541 --> 00:39:59,541
[SPEAKING QUENYA]

566
00:40:00,833 --> 00:40:01,833
[PEOPLE REPEAT IN QUENYA]

567
00:40:03,833 --> 00:40:05,833
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

568
00:40:35,041 --> 00:40:36,041
[SPEAKING QUENYA]

569
00:40:39,166 --> 00:40:40,250
[DOOR SLAMS OPEN]

570
00:40:41,291 --> 00:40:43,499
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

571
00:40:43,500 --> 00:40:47,000
[IN ENGLISH] This shrine is
condemned by order of the king.

572
00:40:47,916 --> 00:40:49,165
Return to your homes.

573
00:40:49,166 --> 00:40:51,624
My son, this is the
oldest shrine in Númenor.

574
00:40:51,625 --> 00:40:53,375
It's in the way of the new aqueduct.

575
00:40:54,083 --> 00:40:56,415
Leave willingly or leave by force.

576
00:40:56,416 --> 00:40:58,375
The King sends his apologies.

577
00:41:07,833 --> 00:41:10,458
How's it feel to have a
daughter who's ashamed of you?

578
00:41:15,625 --> 00:41:18,083
[NÚMENÓREAN GUARD] You
heard him, old man. Out!

579
00:41:21,333 --> 00:41:22,790
[KEMEN] Get his arms.

580
00:41:22,791 --> 00:41:24,291
Wait. Wait!

581
00:41:26,333 --> 00:41:27,625
I'll escort him out.

582
00:41:29,791 --> 00:41:32,575
[IN SINDARIN] If she is not stored,

583
00:41:32,576 --> 00:41:34,208
the souls for whom
she weeps will be lost.

584
00:41:36,958 --> 00:41:38,041
[IN ENGLISH] Give him the relic.

585
00:41:42,416 --> 00:41:43,750
Give it to him, boy.

586
00:42:02,333 --> 00:42:04,915
I don't know if you're aware,
but I've been promoted to...

587
00:42:04,916 --> 00:42:05,958
[GRUNTS]

588
00:42:06,958 --> 00:42:07,958
[COUGHS]

589
00:42:11,666 --> 00:42:12,666
[LAUGHS]

590
00:42:15,791 --> 00:42:17,041
Hold him.

591
00:42:17,750 --> 00:42:18,791
[GRUNTS]

592
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:31,707
This shrine is for The Faithful.
King's men aren't welcome here.

593
00:42:31,708 --> 00:42:33,458
I don't see you praying.

594
00:42:36,916 --> 00:42:38,916
- May the Valar forgive me.
- For what?

595
00:42:39,958 --> 00:42:41,374
No! No!

596
00:42:41,375 --> 00:42:43,375
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

597
00:42:45,791 --> 00:42:48,541
[BOTH GRUNTING]

598
00:42:49,916 --> 00:42:50,916
[ELENDIL] Valandil!

599
00:42:52,750 --> 00:42:54,583
[BOTH GRUNTING]

600
00:43:00,875 --> 00:43:02,166
[GRUNTS]

601
00:43:03,291 --> 00:43:05,166
[ELENDIL] No! Valandil!

602
00:43:07,458 --> 00:43:09,291
[GRUNTING, BREATHING HEAVILY]

603
00:43:10,666 --> 00:43:12,708
[GASPING]

604
00:43:18,708 --> 00:43:20,083
[GRUNTS]

605
00:43:23,583 --> 00:43:24,583
[WOMAN] No!

606
00:43:29,333 --> 00:43:30,541
[GRUNTS]

607
00:43:33,833 --> 00:43:35,250
- [GRUNTS]
- [SCREAMS]

608
00:43:36,291 --> 00:43:38,416
[SCREAMS]

609
00:43:39,541 --> 00:43:40,541
[GASPS]

610
00:43:43,083 --> 00:43:46,000
No! Valandil, put it down!

611
00:43:53,375 --> 00:43:54,458
Put it down, son.

612
00:43:57,375 --> 00:43:59,041
That's an order.

613
00:44:03,875 --> 00:44:05,500
[WHIMPERS]

614
00:44:23,625 --> 00:44:24,708
Aye, Captain.

615
00:44:25,750 --> 00:44:26,750
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

616
00:44:28,583 --> 00:44:29,583
No.

617
00:44:29,584 --> 00:44:31,666
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

618
00:44:41,750 --> 00:44:43,416
[ELENDIL, MUFFLED] No, no, no, no, no.

619
00:44:53,208 --> 00:44:54,208
No.

620
00:45:17,625 --> 00:45:19,250
[ELENDIL WHIMPERING]

621
00:45:32,166 --> 00:45:37,125
Inform the jailer he was the
one who started the uprising.

622
00:45:45,050 --> 00:45:46,083
[CELEBRIMBOR] No!

623
00:45:46,084 --> 00:45:50,124
No, I tell you there is something
wrong with the Dwarven Rings!

624
00:45:50,125 --> 00:45:53,665
Or King Durin is misusing his
Ring and seeking to deflect blame.

625
00:45:53,666 --> 00:45:54,750
[CELEBRIMBOR] No!

626
00:45:55,458 --> 00:45:57,040
No, I do not believe that.

627
00:45:57,041 --> 00:46:00,000
As one who so masterfully
manipulates metals,

628
00:46:00,666 --> 00:46:03,291
just be mindful someone
is not manipulating you.

629
00:46:04,125 --> 00:46:05,874
You see daggers where there are none.

630
00:46:05,875 --> 00:46:09,249
And you ignore them, until
they are right at your throat.

631
00:46:09,250 --> 00:46:10,999
No. Enough.

632
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,500
Did you...

633
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:16,333
in some way...

634
00:46:18,291 --> 00:46:20,291
alter the Dwarven Rings, yes or no?

635
00:46:25,541 --> 00:46:26,625
No.

636
00:46:32,416 --> 00:46:34,041
[CELEBRIMBOR SIGHS]

637
00:46:46,958 --> 00:46:47,958
We did.

638
00:46:49,833 --> 00:46:51,458
What are you talking about?

639
00:46:52,833 --> 00:46:57,250
These are matters of
spirit, as much as craft.

640
00:46:58,375 --> 00:47:01,457
And this time, we brought
deceit into the process.

641
00:47:01,458 --> 00:47:02,875
Deceit?

642
00:47:04,916 --> 00:47:06,458
What deceit could you poss...

643
00:47:09,833 --> 00:47:11,041
The letter.

644
00:47:14,625 --> 00:47:15,625
No.

645
00:47:17,458 --> 00:47:19,333
No, that, that was...

646
00:47:20,333 --> 00:47:21,541
[ANNATAR] You lied.

647
00:47:24,291 --> 00:47:25,999
That was not a lie. I...

648
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:28,333
Your High King consented to the Three.

649
00:47:29,333 --> 00:47:33,999
But the Seven we forged
beneath a cloak of deception.

650
00:47:34,000 --> 00:47:35,666
You must go to Lindon forthwith,

651
00:47:36,541 --> 00:47:38,415
and confess the truth to your High King.

652
00:47:38,416 --> 00:47:40,082
Or matters will worsen.

653
00:47:40,083 --> 00:47:41,750
No, do that, he would...

654
00:47:43,916 --> 00:47:46,416
He would never permit me
to forge anything again.

655
00:47:47,458 --> 00:47:49,083
It is either that,

656
00:47:51,125 --> 00:47:52,875
or we plunge straight on...

657
00:47:55,541 --> 00:47:57,291
even deeper into the maelstrom.

658
00:48:01,250 --> 00:48:04,290
[PRINCE DURIN IV] <i>Father,
I have been to Eregion.</i>

659
00:48:04,291 --> 00:48:09,415
I tell you, some devilry
has gone into these Rings.

660
00:48:09,416 --> 00:48:12,500
We mustn't use them anymore.

661
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:18,624
Time and pressure can shape a Dwarf,

662
00:48:18,625 --> 00:48:21,375
as surely as it can shape a stone.

663
00:48:23,750 --> 00:48:28,082
I had hoped our estrangement
would help shape you, my son.

664
00:48:28,083 --> 00:48:32,915
But I did not expect how
much it would shape me.

665
00:48:32,916 --> 00:48:34,665
- Father...
- I am proud of you.

666
00:48:34,666 --> 00:48:36,416
- No.
- I am proud of you.

667
00:48:37,833 --> 00:48:43,291
Your desire to partner with
the Elves has saved our kingdom.

668
00:48:44,708 --> 00:48:48,375
That is why now, now, more than ever,

669
00:48:49,750 --> 00:48:51,375
I need you.

670
00:48:52,375 --> 00:48:55,458
I need your axe, by my side.

671
00:49:04,083 --> 00:49:05,083
Prince Durin.

672
00:49:13,208 --> 00:49:15,208
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

673
00:49:26,958 --> 00:49:28,082
[DOOR OPENS]

674
00:49:28,083 --> 00:49:29,375
[DISA] Durin?

675
00:49:30,375 --> 00:49:33,000
Durin, what did he say? Did he...

676
00:49:39,125 --> 00:49:40,125
I tried.

677
00:49:40,126 --> 00:49:42,707
But... Durin, no.

678
00:49:42,708 --> 00:49:44,458
I tried to tell him.

679
00:49:46,958 --> 00:49:48,000
Durin...

680
00:49:58,666 --> 00:49:59,666
Swear it.

681
00:50:02,250 --> 00:50:06,458
Swear to me that you will
never wear one of those Rings.

682
00:50:15,750 --> 00:50:17,083
I swear it.

683
00:50:23,916 --> 00:50:28,375
[CELEBRIMBOR] <i>There is agency uncanny
in the heart of stone and ore.</i>

684
00:50:30,041 --> 00:50:33,291
Even when a work is yet within
the artist's bosom, it begins to...

685
00:50:36,333 --> 00:50:37,333
disobey him.

686
00:50:39,875 --> 00:50:42,500
We have failed. Every one of us.

687
00:50:43,041 --> 00:50:47,749
The designs were carried out to
the most exacting detail, my lord.

688
00:50:47,750 --> 00:50:49,125
Were they?

689
00:50:50,458 --> 00:50:53,832
Every last hammer stroke
done to perfection?

690
00:50:53,833 --> 00:50:59,250
Or did, did hubris and sloth come
together to dull your attention?

691
00:51:02,125 --> 00:51:06,290
We must atone for our mistakes
in the only way we can,

692
00:51:06,291 --> 00:51:11,041
by completing the Rings together.

693
00:51:13,625 --> 00:51:17,082
The Nine must do far more
than bring aid to Men,

694
00:51:17,083 --> 00:51:20,207
they must bring balance
to the entire project.

695
00:51:20,208 --> 00:51:24,000
They must draw strength from the Three.

696
00:51:24,625 --> 00:51:25,875
And somehow...

697
00:51:28,291 --> 00:51:29,958
redeem the Seven.

698
00:51:32,958 --> 00:51:36,000
They must redeem us all.

699
00:51:39,208 --> 00:51:41,583
We shall work night and day.

700
00:51:43,166 --> 00:51:47,625
New designs. New alloys. A new process.

701
00:51:48,625 --> 00:51:50,332
I will be with you at every turn.

702
00:51:50,333 --> 00:51:54,749
And any of you who offers so
much as a hair's breadth less

703
00:51:54,750 --> 00:51:58,165
than his utmost effort is a s...

704
00:51:58,166 --> 00:52:00,375
A smith of Eregion no longer.

705
00:52:03,458 --> 00:52:04,999
Have I made myself plain?

706
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:06,791
[ALL] Yes, yes, my lord.

707
00:52:07,541 --> 00:52:08,625
It starts now.

708
00:52:14,666 --> 00:52:16,290
[MIRDANIA, SOFTLY] What
has gotten into him?

709
00:52:16,291 --> 00:52:18,249
[HUSHED CHATTER]

710
00:52:18,250 --> 00:52:21,916
My friends. Do not be discouraged.

711
00:52:24,291 --> 00:52:28,166
Your master may seem unreasonable.

712
00:52:29,833 --> 00:52:34,208
His demands intemperate,
or even impossible.

713
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:39,416
But that is simply because he knows
how much depends on your success.

714
00:52:40,375 --> 00:52:42,916
Yet, I know you will not disappoint him.

715
00:52:43,291 --> 00:52:45,458
[BREATH TREMBLES, SIGHS]

716
00:52:47,041 --> 00:52:48,250
[ANNATAR] Or me.

717
00:52:52,208 --> 00:52:54,875
I, for one, am certain

718
00:52:56,250 --> 00:52:58,374
that we will complete
the Rings of Power.

719
00:52:58,375 --> 00:52:59,458
[ELVEN SMITH 1] Yes.

720
00:53:04,750 --> 00:53:05,957
Shall we begin?

721
00:53:05,958 --> 00:53:07,458
[ELVEN SMITH 1] Yes, of course, my lord.

722
00:53:08,791 --> 00:53:09,791
Lord of Gifts indeed.

723
00:53:10,666 --> 00:53:12,540
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

724
00:53:12,541 --> 00:53:13,625
[ELVEN SMITH 2] Let's get to it.

725
00:53:28,416 --> 00:53:31,374
[ORCS SNARLING AND GROWLING]

726
00:53:31,375 --> 00:53:33,458
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

727
00:53:58,875 --> 00:54:00,083
[ELROND] High King!

728
00:54:01,583 --> 00:54:04,583
High King, the Orcs are not in Mordor.

729
00:54:05,083 --> 00:54:07,333
A legion of them are headed for Eregion.

730
00:54:07,833 --> 00:54:09,040
Galadriel was right.

731
00:54:09,041 --> 00:54:12,125
You must send the army
to Eregion this moment.

732
00:54:13,375 --> 00:54:15,041
That will not be possible.

733
00:54:15,541 --> 00:54:21,250
I have reason to believe that
Sauron is the architect of all this.

734
00:54:22,166 --> 00:54:26,249
High King, Eregion is the
very jewel of Elvendom.

735
00:54:26,250 --> 00:54:29,415
If it were to fall, it would be a
mortal blow for all in Middle-earth.

736
00:54:29,416 --> 00:54:31,208
You must send aid!

737
00:54:32,208 --> 00:54:36,332
Our armies cannot defeat
both Adar and Sauron.

738
00:54:36,333 --> 00:54:37,666
Not alone.

739
00:54:38,125 --> 00:54:40,749
[ORCS LAUGHING AND SNARLING]

740
00:54:40,750 --> 00:54:44,082
[ORC 1] Come on! Come on!

741
00:54:44,083 --> 00:54:46,291
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

742
00:54:58,000 --> 00:54:59,208
[ORC, IN BLACK SPEECH] Back away!

743
00:55:00,875 --> 00:55:02,125
[SNARLING]

744
00:55:08,916 --> 00:55:11,958
[ORCS LAUGHING]

745
00:55:21,041 --> 00:55:23,416
[ORCS EXCLAIMING]

746
00:55:26,833 --> 00:55:27,833
[ORC, IN ENGLISH] Get her out.

747
00:55:29,091 --> 00:55:30,125
[ORCS SNARLING]

748
00:55:30,126 --> 00:55:32,290
- [ORC 2] Look out for her.
- [ORC 3] It's okay.

749
00:55:32,291 --> 00:55:33,665
[ORCS 4] Yeah.

750
00:55:33,666 --> 00:55:34,708
[GRUNTS]

751
00:55:44,458 --> 00:55:47,250
[ORCS EXCLAIMING]

752
00:55:51,916 --> 00:55:53,125
[ADAR, IN SINDARIN] I brought you here

753
00:55:54,125 --> 00:55:55,208
not as a prisoner...

